From: Senior Matthew <SeniorMatt@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 22 Nov 2026 01:29:33 +0500
Subject: [PATCH 2/9] kinfocenter info pages: one shared look and a lighter
 first frame (CommandOutputContext, CommandOutputKCM)

Base of 17 read-only information pages (cpu, edid, egl, glx, vulkan, opencl, vaapi, wayland, xserver, kwinsupportinfo,
pci, usb, network, interrupts, sensors, audio_information, block_devices, firmware_security); memory moves onto it in a
later commit. Page type: "Info" (a Form/List variant in docs/page-design.md: the output is the page, toolbar on top).

Look (docs/page-design.md 2, 3, 7; HIG-001/005):
- The text uses Kirigami.Theme.fixedWidthFont like every other mono text in Plasma (was the literal family "monospace",
  and kcm_memory used the theme font: now all pages the same).
- Busy indicator after 150 ms (was 500), as the design says for every page.
- Filter applies while typing (150 ms pause, Enter at once); before only Enter did anything.
- New toolbar action "Refresh" (F5) on snapshot pages (those without auto refresh); it also retries after an error.
  Copy to Clipboard, Filter (Ctrl+I) and Pause/Resume Refreshing are unchanged.
- "Report to <distribution>" only for a missing or crashing tool (errorReportable) and only when the distribution has a
  bug report URL; the button used to be offered for every error.

Speed (cause found in code): CommandOutputContext's constructor called load() directly (QMetaObject::invokeMethod on the
same thread is a direct call), so inside page creation it ran executable lookup (QStandardPaths on PATH plus sbin dirs),
KOSRelease() (parses /etc/os-release, once more in the constructor for the bug URL) and started the process. Now load() is
queued (starts after the page exists), and bugReportUrl is read lazily when the button is used. A tool that cannot be
started (errorOccurred FailedToStart) used to leave the page on the busy indicator forever; it now reports the error. A
second run while one is still going (1 s auto refresh with a slow tool, double Refresh) is skipped.
New manual mode (CommandOutputContext(QObject*), setOutput/setFailure, refreshRequested) for pages whose data does not
come from a process (memory, via KAuth).
After numbers: pending, manager will measure.

Not built yet (heavy work stopped); checked statically. Uncertain: StandardKey.Refresh as Kirigami.Action.shortcut (same pattern in bluedevil ForgetDeviceDialog.qml:65 and
about-distro main.qml:151, but not confirmed for Refresh).

